            "creation_time": "2026-10-23T11:42:03Z",
            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19245,
            "text": "Created attachment 3946\nsuggested fix and regression test\n\nIn many cases, the repositories in `getOption('repos')` are specified without the trailing directory separator. Since `utils:::available_packages_filters_db$CRAN` checks for CRAN packages using `startsWith()`, this makes it possible for a domain that uses CRAN as a prefix to be confused with CRAN:\n\n```\noptions(repos = c(CRAN = CRAN <- 'https://cloud.r-project.org'))\nnotCRAN <- paste0(CRAN, '.example.invalid')\ndb <- cbind(\n Package = 'pkg',\n Version = c('1.0', '2.0'),\n Repository = contrib.url(c(CRAN, notCRAN), 'source')\n)\ndb |>\n utils:::available_packages_filters_db$CRAN() |>\n utils:::available_packages_filters_db$duplicates()\n#      Package Version Repository\n# [1,] \"pkg\"   \"2.0\"   \"https://cloud.r-project.org.example.invalid/src/contrib\"\n```\n\nThis is not a vulnerability because the repositories in `getOption('repos')` should always be considered trusted, with or without filters.\n\nTested with `LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 TZ=UTC make check-devel`.",
            "attachment_id": 3946,
            "time": "2026-10-23T11:42:03Z",
            "creator": "ikrylov",
            "is_markdown": true
          }
        ]
      }
    }
